 "notes": "Main line: Er screen (UV-vis, UC) -> Er0.5 down-select -> Ce series -> band gap/PL/EIS -> dye degradation -> antibacterial ranking correlated with photocatalysis -> ROS mechanism. Packet F-ids differ from paper numbers (packet F8 = paper Fig. 8 but F9 = paper Fig. 7; F1 = Scheme 1). Image audit: F4a rutile reflections fade with Ce and are absent for Ce0.3, while text attributes the change to 'annealing temperature' and calls all samples mixed-phase (b16 contradicts); F6 Ce 3d/Er 4d XPS is noise-level, so the Ce3+/Ce4+ claim that feeds both the carrier-trap and the dark-kill mechanism has no image support (b20/b21 not_shown); F9 EIS/photocurrent partial; F10 dark vs light bars show that the doped samples' advantage is largely light-independent (b37 text_silent), which weakens the photocatalysis->killing inference the paper draws by correlating F8 with F10 (correlate_across_figures). PRP family 'catalytic' is missing from the family list. Lost: Raman (F4d, 700 C samples, broad ~620 cm-1 band text-silent), EDS C dominance, survey XPS.",
 "migrated_from": "r02/graphs/Bioactive_Materials__j.bioactmat.2020.02.005.json"
